; DVD-logo-style bouncing smiley for 64x48 screen
; Registers: R0=x, R1=y, R2=vx, R3=vy, R4/R5=previous position, R6/R7=scratch, R8=pixel address, R9=first-frame flag.
; Yellow face (palette index 3), black eyes and smile (palette index 0).
; Uses CPU instructions for motion, collisions, and every pixel write.
; Jump targets are absolute ROM cell addresses (3 cells per instruction).
LDI 0 12 ; x
LDI 1 9 ; y
LDI 2 1 ; horizontal speed
LDI 3 1 ; vertical speed
; FRAME (PC=12)
CMPEI 9 0
JCMP 6318 0 ; if first frame, skip erase
COP 4 6
ADDI 6 7
COP 5 7
ADDI 7 0
BLT 6 7
BLTR 8 0
VSTI 8 0 ; erase previous sprite
COP 4 6
ADDI 6 4
COP 5 7
ADDI 7 1
BLT 6 7
BLTR 8 0
VSTI 8 0 ; erase previous sprite
COP 4 6
ADDI 6 5
COP 5 7
ADDI 7 1
BLT 6 7
BLTR 8 0
